{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++11 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include<cstdio>\n#include<algorithm> \n#include<cstring>\n#define LL long long\nusing namespace std;\nconst int N=65;\nconst int mod=1e9+7;\nint m,len;\nLL n,v[N];\nstruct node\n{\n\tint v[35][35];\n\tnode(){memset(v,0,sizeof(v));}\n}S,T[N][35],s1[N][35],s2[N][35];\nnode operator * (node a,node b)\n{\n\tnode c;\n\tfor(int i=0;i<=m;i++)\n\t\tfor(int j=0;j<=m;j++)\n\t\t\tfor(int k=0;k<=m;k++)\n\t\t\t\tc.v[i][j]=(c.v[i][j]+1ll*a.v[i][k]*b.v[k][j]%mod)%mod;\n\treturn c;\n}\nint main()\n{\n\tscanf(\"%lld%d\",&n,&m);\n\tv[0]=n;while(v[len])v[len+1]=v[len]/m,v[len]%=m,len++;\n\tfor(int i=0;i<len;i++)\n\t{\n\t\tif(!i)\n\t\t{\n\t\t\tfor(int j=0;j<m;j++)\n\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\tT[i][j].v[m][m]=1;\n\t\t\t\tfor(int a=0;a<m;a++)\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\tif(a!=j){T[i][j].v[a][a]=1;continue;}\n\t\t\t\t\tfor(int b=0;b<=m;b++)T[i][j].v[a][b]=1;\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\telse\n\t\t{\n\t\t\tfor(int j=0;j<m;j++)\n\t\t\t\tif(!j)T[i][j]=s2[i-1][0];\n\t\t\t\telse T[i][j]=s2[i-1][j]*s1[i-1][j-1];\n\t\t}\n\t\ts1[i][0]=T[i][0];\n\t\tfor(int j=1;j<m;j++)s1[i][j]=s1[i][j-1]*T[i][j];\n\t\ts2[i][m-1]=T[i][m-1];\n\t\tfor(int j=m-2;j>=0;j--)s2[i][j]=T[i][j]*s2[i][j+1];\n\t}\n\tfor(int i=0;i<=m;i++)S.v[0][i]=1;\n\tfor(int i=len-1,j=0;i>=0;i--)\n\t\twhile(v[i]--)S=S*T[i][j],j=(j+1)%m;\n\tprintf(\"%d\",S.v[0][m]);\n\treturn 0;\n}\n\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\n\nMOD = 1000000007\n\ndef mat_mul(A, B):\n    m = len(A) - 1\n    C = [[0] * (m+1) for _ in range(m+1)]\n    for i in range(m+1):\n        for k in range(m+1):\n            aik = A[i][k]\n            if aik:\n                for j in range(m+1):\n                    C[i][j] = (C[i][j] + aik * B[k][j]) % MOD\n    return C\n\ndef solve():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().strip().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    n = int(data[0])\n    m = int(data[1])\n    if n == 0:\n        print(1)\n        return\n\n    # convert n to base m digits, least significant first\n    digits = []\n    temp = n\n    while temp > 0:\n        digits.append(temp % m)\n        temp //= m\n    L = len(digits)\n\n    T = [None] * L\n    s1 = [None] * L\n    s2 = [None] * L\n\n    for i in range(L):\n        T_i = []\n        if i == 0:\n            for j in range(m):\n                mat = [[0] * (m+1) for _ in range(m+1)]\n                # T[i][j].v[m][m] = 1\n                mat[m][m] = 1\n                for a in range(m):\n                    if a != j:\n                        mat[a][a] = 1\n                    else:\n                        for b in range(m+1):\n                            mat[a][b] = 1\n                T_i.append(mat)\n        else:\n            for j in range(m):\n                if j == 0:\n                    # reference to s2[i-1][0] is fine as it is never mutated\n                    T_i.append(s2[i-1][0])\n                else:\n                    T_i.append(mat_mul(s2[i-1][j], s1[i-1][j-1]))\n        T[i] = T_i\n\n        # compute s1[i]\n        s1_i = [None] * m\n        s1_i[0] = T_i[0]  # reference\n        for j in range(1, m):\n            s1_i[j] = mat_mul(s1_i[j-1], T_i[j])\n        s1[i] = s1_i\n\n        # compute s2[i]\n        s2_i = [None] * m\n        s2_i[m-1] = T_i[m-1]  # reference\n        for j in range(m-2, -1, -1):\n            s2_i[j] = mat_mul(T_i[j], s2_i[j+1])\n        s2[i] = s2_i\n\n    # S is a row vector of size m+1 (first row all 1, rest 0)\n    S = [[0] * (m+1) for _ in range(m+1)]\n    for i in range(m+1):\n        S[0][i] = 1\n\n    j = 0\n    for i in range(L-1, -1, -1):\n        d = digits[i]\n        for _ in range(d):\n            S = mat_mul(S, T[i][j])\n            j = (j + 1) % m\n\n    print(S[0][m] % MOD)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.98\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-4.7444173105759546e-05, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.0003830652858596295, -0.8405506014823914, -4.589452510117553e-05, -0.014194007031619549, -0.10771159827709198, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.0002615109842736274, -0.201687753200531, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.00016830935783218592, -1.8596476365928538e-05, -0.000927137560211122, -2.47952248173533e-05, 0.0, -0.0024781490210443735, -3.3378546504536644e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.47420674562454224, -2.7418097943154862e-06, -1.3903446197509766, -0.037773873656988144, -1.9073468138230965e-06, -3.5523738915799186e-05, -0.0001037067049765028, -5.602820692729438e-06, -5.960462772236497e-07, -2.9802276912960224e-06, -0.9743500351905823, -9.536738616588991e-07, -0.004383479245007038, 0.0, -7.867782187531702e-06, 0.0, -2.6702524337451905e-05, -0.038041528314352036, -4.768370445162873e-07, -1.1086402082582936e-05, -1.136871576309204, -0.0002964295563288033, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -7.152555099310121e-07, 0.0, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -5.960462772236497e-07, -2.264974000354414e-06, 0.0, -1.6569954823353328e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.